# Commenting Standard: Doxygen

## File Headers (every .c and .h)

```c
/**
 * @file    filename.c
 * @brief   One-line summary of the module's purpose.
 * @details What it does, why it exists, who feeds it (upstream), who consumes it (downstream).
 * @author  Madhu
 * @date    YYYY-MM-DD
 */
```

## Function Documentation (every non-static public function)

```c
/**
 * @brief  One-line summary of what the function does.
 * @details Expanded explanation: algorithm, hardware interaction, timing constraints.
 *
 * @param[in]  name   Description (units, valid range, alignment requirements).
 * @param[out] name   Description (what gets written, who reads it).
 * @param[in,out] name  Description.
 *
 * @return Type  What the return value means (e.g., HAL_OK on success).
 *
 * @note   Hardware gotchas, errata workarounds, non-obvious constraints.
 * @pre    What must be true before calling (e.g., "SPI1 must be idle").
 * @post   What is guaranteed after return (e.g., "DMA TC interrupt armed").
 * @see    Related functions, datasheet sections, RM0481 references.
 */
```

## Inline Comments

- Only for non-obvious logic, hardware quirks, errata references, or datasheet citations.
- Reference datasheet sections: `/* See ADS131M02 datasheet Table 25, Section 9.5.2 */`
- Never narrate what code obviously does (`/* increment counter */` is forbidden).

## Tags to Always Use

`@brief`, `@param[in/out]`, `@return`, `@note` (gotchas), `@pre`/`@post`, `@see` (cross-refs).

# Naming Conventions

| Category | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `#define` constants | `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` | `ADC_FRAME_SIZE_BYTES` |
| `enum` values | `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` | `ADC_STATE_IDLE` |
| `const` variables | `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` | `MAX_CHANNEL_COUNT` |
| Functions | `camelCase` | `ads131m02Init()` |
| Local variables | `camelCase` | `frameCount` |
| Global variables | `g_` prefix + `camelCase` | `g_adcReady` |
| Struct/typedef names | `camelCase_t` | `adcConfig_t` |
| Struct members | `camelCase` | `.sampleRate` |
| Module prefix | `lowercase` | `ads131m02_`, `lsm6dsv_` |

Do NOT rename HAL/CubeMX-generated identifiers (e.g., `hspi1`, `HAL_GPIO_ReadPin`). Only apply these conventions to application code we write.
